{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Problem\n\nTab order (the *slot* a page occupies, shown in the header as `n:Label`) is fixed by the registration order in `src/main.rs` and cannot be expressed in the config. Keybindings (`app { \"7\" \"page:worktrees\" }`) address pages by name and are independent of slots, so while a page is missing (e.g. Actions not yet merged) the header reads `6:Worktrees` although the key is `7`. Deriving the header number from the bound key was tried in #113 and rejected: a page is assigned to a slot, and keybindings are operations on that assignment — not the other way round.\n\n## Spec\n\n- New top-level node `pages \"git\" \"github\" \"files\" \"docker\" \"procs\" \"actions\" \"worktrees\"`: the listed order defines slots 1..n and the header shows `n:Label`. When omitted the builtin order applies.\n- A user config's `pages` replaces the builtin list wholesale (same rule as `layout`). Pages not listed are disabled (not registered) — e.g. `pages \"git\" \"files\" \"worktrees\"` gives a three-tab vig.\n- `app { \"<key>\" \"page:<name>\" }` keeps addressing pages by name; the builtin defaults bind each slot number to its page. Bindings to pages that are not in `pages` are an error.\n- The help overlay's \"Switch view\" row is generated from the `app` bindings (`1 / 2 / … / 7`; a user rebinding `\"w\" \"page:worktrees\"` shows `w`).\n- Unknown or duplicate page names in `pages` are errors (fail fast with file and line, like other config errors).\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [ ] `Config::pages()` in `src/core/config/loader.rs` (+ validation in `with_user`, tests)\n- [ ] `merge.rs`: `pages` is a replace-wholesale top-level node\n- [ ] `src/main.rs`: build pages by name, then order / filter them by `pages`; `App` / header consume the slot order\n- [ ] `docs/config.md` (+ README mention), CLAUDE.md \"How to add a page\" (register the name in the builtin `pages` list)\n- [ ] Tests: builtin order, reordering, disabling a page, unknown / duplicate names, binding to a disabled page\n","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-28T09:13:09Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":114,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Config: explicit page slots via a top-level `pages` node"}
